      "natural_statement": "Completion is exact; completed finite constructions admit strict realization by perfect operation modules, and maps between the relevant objects induce continuous overlap maps (complete:fracture, complete:realization, complete:topology).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "2ea2c6cd5677d1996bf02061bffea6627abe5bd501dee23d0fffcb6992fb4bcf"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_ANNIHILATOR_REMOVAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000319",
        "content_hash": "f36c1fff769140d49662a1a73b61d35a5be680bd0c8890d3704e6db9244aab7d"
      },
      "natural_statement": "A right x-saturated ideal J containing a Delta with JS=S has an integral member whose reduced symbol is outside (C); separately, an operator outside Sa annihilating V in ker(a) yields an integral annihilator of V with reduced symbol outside (C) (obs:right-annihilator).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "6ff0a08c945dbfaf4024b9b1926573177d2d146fa4c3dc541573b2717a4a2e6c"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_ADJOINT",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000319",
        "content_hash": "f36c1fff769140d49662a1a73b61d35a5be680bd0c8890d3704e6db9244aab7d"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The constant-term pairing gives every integral operator an integral adjoint; reduction induces group inversion and preserves both symbol conditions of obs:growth (obs:adjoint).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "4c5e6115175693f7e394797845e7527fc4b5d0cf6dfe99d3f870004e04a38432"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_GLOBAL_MAPS",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000319",
        "content_hash": "f36c1fff769140d49662a1a73b61d35a5be680bd0c8890d3704e6db9244aab7d"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Global maps out of the glued object preserve the discrete overlap lattice images needed in the paired-lattice argument (glue:global-maps).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "4403de2a02e7d410a4732c5643f078d26abb51c57ffd2163e376e579774fa77f"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_PERIODIC_SPLITTING",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000319",
        "content_hash": "f36c1fff769140d49662a1a73b61d35a5be680bd0c8890d3704e6db9244aab7d"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Over a left and right principal domain, finite modules split into finite free and torsion parts with free resolution length at most one; perfect positive-even-periodic dg modules split into periodizations of homology (obs:periodic-splitting).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "bce12f8e3ab4b180741c765672b3a22dd602f64e0d4973a4f834be080edcefa0"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_TOWER_NORMAL_FORM",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000319",
        "content_hash": "f36c1fff769140d49662a1a73b61d35a5be680bd0c8890d3704e6db9244aab7d"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Every object in Thick(T_0) is a retract of a finite tower whose layers are finite sums of arbitrary shifts of T_0 (rew:obs:tower-normal-form).",
